--TEST--
Core\Storage refuses a `$disk` no `[storage.<name>]` block gives a `root`, and fails over a `root` that is there and is not a directory — ADR 0082 § 2
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Two refusals with nothing between them, and they are different in kind: the
// first is about `nvs.toml` and happens before any door is asked, the second is
// about the disk and happens after the grant has already opened one.
//
// The first, in three spellings that are one sentence. No block of that name, a
// block that sets no `root`, and a `root` an operator cleared are all "there is
// no disk of that name": `crates/nvs-stdlib/src/storage.rs`'s `root_of` reads
// blank as absent on purpose, since a `root = ""` read as a directory would
// produce a refusal about the working directory rather than about the
// configuration.
array<string> $nameless = ["missing", "empty", "blank"];
foreach ($nameless as string $disk) {
    try {
        Core\Storage::get($disk, "note.txt");
        echo "reached a disk with no root: ", $disk, "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $error) {
        echo $error->message, "\n";
    }
}

// The second. `root` names something that exists and is a file, and the `fs.*`
// grant covers it — so nothing about configuration or capability is wrong and
// the door opens onto a path the operating system will not read as a directory.
// That is an `IOError`, and this case names the class rather than the wording:
// the sentence inside it is the host's own and differs between them.
try {
    Core\Storage::list("broken");
    echo "listed a disk whose root is a file", "\n";
} catch (IOError $failure) {
    echo "list: IOError", "\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[storage.empty]

[storage.blank]
root = ""

[storage.broken]
root = "./notes.txt"

[capabilities.fs]
read = ["./notes.txt"]
write = ["./notes.txt"]
--FILE notes.txt--
a file, where the deployment said a directory
--EXPECT--
Core\Storage::get: no `[storage.missing]` block sets `root`, so there is no disk of that name to store on
Core\Storage::get: no `[storage.empty]` block sets `root`, so there is no disk of that name to store on
Core\Storage::get: no `[storage.blank]` block sets `root`, so there is no disk of that name to store on
list: IOError
